Flayr Chop patch for JUCE 8.0.16-security (ea77444750de45e036e0279bb0291144bf8e3688).

CAF metadata (CoreAudioFormatMetatdata, macOS): a chunk with a negative size
moved the stream backwards and the chunk loop never ended (a 20-byte file hung the
loader), and the 'info' and 'uuid' chunk parsers looped up to a 32-bit entry count
from the file after the stream ran out. Found by Flayr Chop's fuzzing.

Applied by CMakeLists.txt via FetchContent PATCH_COMMAND (cmake/ApplyPatch.cmake).

Flayr-Patch-Marker: modules/juce_audio_formats/codecs/juce_CoreAudioFormat.cpp Flayr Chop: negative chunk size
Flayr-Patch-Marker: modules/juce_audio_formats/codecs/juce_CoreAudioFormat.cpp Flayr Chop: info entries
Flayr-Patch-Marker: modules/juce_audio_formats/codecs/juce_CoreAudioFormat.cpp Flayr Chop: uuid entries

